# Hardware

The XMPL100's pins, transfer function and power, as the driver uses them.

## Pins

| Pin | Direction | Function |
| --- | --- | --- |
| VDD | Power | Supply; 100 nF to GND at the pin |
| GND | Power | |
| VOUT | Out | Analog output to an MCU ADC channel |
| SHDN_N | In | Shutdown, active low; optional (`CtrlPin::Enable`) |

## Transfer function

| Parameter | Symbol | Value | Driver |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Output at 0 °C | V_0 | 500 mV typical | `Config::offset_mv` |
| Slope | T_C | 10 mV/°C typical | `Config::slope_uv_per_c` |
| Output range | | 100 mV to 1750 mV | `kOutputMinMv`, `kOutputMaxMv` |
| Power-on time | t_ON | 800 µs maximum | `kPowerOnTimeUs` |

A reading outside the output range at `Initialize()` is `DeviceIdMismatch` (no sensor on the channel); later it is
`DeviceFault` (output open or shorted).

